  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Living Conditions of Conflict and Disaster Affected Populations in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the beginning of 2023, Somalia has been impacted by interlinked crises. While still affected by one of the most severe droughts in the last decades that has driven mass displacement, widespread death of livestock and a devastating food and water crisis, the country is now also receiving heavy rains which are causing flash floods and increased risk of riverine flooding in some areas. The main objective of this project is to ensure dignified, safe and secure living conditions and basic services for vulnerable populations affected by man-made and natural disasters in Somalia. IOM proposes an integrated emergency support intervention, including Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), Protection, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and Multi-Purpose Cash.</narrative>
  </description>
